usage: planner_worker.py [-h] [--serve] [--ready READY]
                         [--grasp-repo GRASP_REPO]
                         [--robosuite-assets ROBOSUITE_ASSETS]
                         [--request REQUEST] [--response RESPONSE]

Persistent cuRobo worker for the independent LIBERO bridge. No GPU is
initialized until a configure request is received. Commands: configure:
{scene, calibration_samples, output_dir} plan_pose: {scene, goal_pose,
out_dir, timeout_s?, allow_target_contact?, ignore_obstacles?:
[exact_geom_name]} select: {scene, candidates:[{world_T_eef,score,...}],
out_dir, max_candidates?, approach_distance_m?, allow_target_contact?} attach:
{scene}; detach: {}; status: {} Each plan returns path_file; NPZ has
q_arm[N,7], world_T_eef[N,4,4]. select also returns approach_path_file /
descend_path_file. Coordinates are meters and world-frame control-site
transforms. No Isaac modules are used.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --serve
  --ready READY
  --grasp-repo GRASP_REPO
                        Accepted for bridge launcher compatibility; no Isaac
                        code is imported
  --robosuite-assets ROBOSUITE_ASSETS
  --request REQUEST     Run one JSON request (use --serve for a persistent
                        planner)
  --response RESPONSE
